/home/eddyilg/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/torch/include/c10/util/complex.h:8:10: fatal error: thrust/complex.h: No such file or directory
As fas as I know, with CUDA 11 thrust was removed. What I am wondering about:
1.) Pytorch seems to include parts of CUDA 10 in the folder "torch/include/c10", however they don't include thrust. I am wondering how this can work?
2.) The pytorch version is compiled against CUDA 11 but still has a version 10 folder "torch/include/c10" that references thrust externally (which is not present in CUDA 11). Also here I don't understand how this can work.
Note that in my /usr/include/cuda folder there is a "thrust" folder with the following contents:
async
cmake
detail
iterator
mr
random
system
type_traits
However, it is missing complex.h.
Could someone help me out what could be wrong and why the torch CUDA references thrust but doesn't include it? Thanks in advance

